### IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client. Execute from top to bottom against docker compose.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Register a customer. Use a new email if running again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Olena Kovalenko","email":"olena.lab1@example.com"}

> {% client.global.set("customerId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Create a product. Use a new SKU if running again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{"sku":"KEYBOARD-001","name":"Mechanical keyboard","description":"USB keyboard","price":1500.00,"stock":10}

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=0&size=20

### 4. Update product
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Mechanical keyboard","description":"Updated description","price":1600.00}

### 5. Place an order; server calculates the total
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId":"{{customerId}}","items":[{"productId":"{{productId}}","quantity":2}]}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### 6. Read order (also execute after docker compose restart db)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### 7. Customer order history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?customerId={{customerId}}&page=0&size=20

### 8. Expected 409: not enough stock
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId":"{{customerId}}","items":[{"productId":"{{productId}}","quantity":1000}]}

### 9. Cancel; repeat to verify stock is not restored twice
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel

### 10. Restock
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/restock
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":5}

### 11. Soft delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### 12. Database-aware health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
